## 1. What the app is

- A static HTML/CSS/vanilla JS front end (no build step) with a Google Apps Script backend (`apps-script/Code.gs`) that stores data in Google Sheets and Drive.
- **Guest pages:** `index.html`, `register.html`, `signin.html`, `photos.html`, `ceremony.html`, `gift.html`, `games.html`, `pass.html`, `memorial.html`, `slideshow.html`, `whisper.html`.
- **Admin pages:** `admin/index.html`, `admin/planner.html`, `admin/nametags.html`.
- **Scripts:** `js/config.js`, `js/api.js`, `js/app.js`, `js/i18n.js`, `js/admin.js`, `js/register.js`, `js/photos.js`, `js/ceremony.js`, `js/gift.js`, `js/games.js`, `js/pass.js`, `js/memorial.js`, `js/planner.js`, `js/nametags.js`, `sw.js`.

### Demo and production modes

- `js/config.js` picks the mode. It honours `?mode=demo` or `?mode=prod` and remembers the choice in localStorage `appMode`. Without that, it defaults to demo on localhost/file URLs and to prod everywhere else.
- **Demo mode** loads `demo-data/demo-api.js`, an in-browser fake backend. Its data is kept in localStorage `demoDB`, and guest `G001` is signed in automatically. Demo invite codes are `DEMO01` to `DEMO06`.
- **Production mode** posts to the Apps Script `/exec` URL. `API_URL` in `js/config.js` is still `PASTE_YOUR_APPS_SCRIPT_WEB_APP_URL_HERE`.
- `start-demo.ps1` starts a Python server on port 8080 and opens the app in Chrome.

### Admin passcode

- **Demo:** `demo`. `js/api.js` blocks admin calls unless `sessionStorage.adminKey === 'demo'`.
- **Production owner:** Script Property `ADMIN_PASSCODE`. `setup()` sets it to `change-me-now`, which must be changed before going live.
- **Other production admins:** each has their own passcode in the `Admins` sheet (managed from the Team tab).
- **Roles:** `owner` can do everything. `manager` can do everything except settings, admins and logs. `helper` gets a limited list of actions (see `roleAllows_` in `Code.gs`).

